\documentclass[11pt]{article}

\usepackage[review]{acl}

\usepackage{times}
\usepackage{latexsym}
\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}
\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}
\usepackage{microtype}
\usepackage{inconsolata}
\usepackage{graphicx}
\usepackage{booktabs}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{amssymb}
\usepackage{amsthm}
\newtheorem{proposition}{Proposition}
\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}
\newtheorem{corollary}{Corollary}
\newtheorem{definition}{Definition}
\usepackage{multirow}
\usepackage{xcolor}
\usepackage{subcaption}
\usepackage{alphalph}

\graphicspath{{figures/}}

\title{The Capability Ceiling of Self-Consistency:\\ Why Entity-Level Self-Verification Fails in Structured Generation}

\author{Anonymous}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\input{sections/abstract}
\input{sections/introduction}
\input{sections/diagnostic}
\input{sections/mechanistic}
\input{sections/single_signal}
\input{sections/adaptive}
\input{sections/theory}
\input{sections/experiments_main}
\input{sections/background}
\input{sections/discussion}
\input{sections/conclusion}

\section*{Limitations}
\input{sections/limitations}

\section*{Ethics Statement}
All experiments use publicly available benchmarks (SciERC, CoNLL-2003, WNUT-17) and open-weight models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-4B, LLaMA-3.1-8B).
CoNLL-2003 is derived from the Reuters RCV1 corpus, which is available for research purposes under a NIST agreement; we use the standard research distribution.
No new human data was collected or annotated for this study.
Our findings on signal limitations could inform more reliable deployment of IE systems by guiding practitioners toward appropriate confidence signals for their use case.
Code and data will be released upon acceptance at [anonymized URL].

\section*{Responsible NLP Research Checklist}
\input{sections/checklist}

\bibliography{references}

\appendix
\renewcommand{\thesection}{\alphalph{\value{section}}}
\input{sections/appendix}

\end{document}

\section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}

NER exhibits oracle scaling comparable to reasoning ($c{\approx}0.5$) but aggregation fails: a degeneracy decomposition ($\theta_{\text{crit}}{=}0.70$; \S\ref{sec:theory}) formalizes when SC becomes futile.
Entity-level construction partially closes the gap ($+1.40$\,pp Few-NERD, $+1.02$\,pp SciERC); a trained verifier achieves AUC${=}0.92$ but yields only $+0.30$\,pp via OOF construction, with negative cross-dataset transfer---content-aware methods \cite{cobbe2021verifiers} may bridge this.

